YODPAY: An Edge-First Protocol for Fault-Tolerant, Offline-First Value Transfer

Author: Sibongakonke Masondo
Architecture: Gideon Mesh Labs
Version: 1.0.0 (Production Blueprint)

1. Executive Abstract

Traditional retail payment networks operate on an immutable architectural premise: permanent, low-latency access to a centralized, cloud-hosted ledger or distributed state machine. In environments subject to infrastructure degradation, power shedding, or physical routing isolation, this design introduces single points of failure.

YODPAY introduces an edge-first protocol suite that decouples transaction execution from immediate backend server settlement. By leveraging localized, adaptive Byzantine Fault Tolerant (BFT) consensus thresholds, strict hardware-isolated sequential nonces, and dynamic risk-tier mapping, YODPAY guarantees zero-downtime value transfer within fully partitioned, zero-connectivity topologies. It achieves deterministic local finality on untrusted edge devices while maintaining cryptographic safety guarantees against double-spending upon network reintegration.

2. The Edge-First Core Philosophy

YODPAY is built for environments where the network is treated as a highly volatile runtime variable rather than a constant. The architecture treats physical isolation as a normal operational state, moving the transaction validation engine closer to the mesh edge.

